# Design reference material — kept on disk, deliberately out of git.
# 128 MB of .mp4/.gif clips and a deliverables zip. Git cannot diff video, so a
# binary that large never shrinks: it is carried by every clone and every Vercel
# build forever, and removing it later means rewriting history. It is reference,
# not source — nothing in the build reads it.
design/reference/

# Raw career/source material for the case studies — ON DISK, NEVER COMMITTED.
# This repo is public. These are ChatGPT transcripts containing a personal phone
# number and private addresses, compensation and severance discussion, an active
# job search naming current and prospective employers, and a confidential
# conversation about laying off a named-adjacent report who held a medical
# accommodation. Publishing any of it would harm John and a third party who never
# consented. It is INPUT to step 3, not output: what ships is the written case
# study in content/, which cites none of this.
content/source/

# Raw resume source (docx + extracted OOXML) — ON DISK, NEVER COMMITTED.
# Contains a personal phone number in plaintext. "Phone held for the PDF, not the
# page" (docs/HANDOFF_README.md) means kept off the rendered site — committing the
# source to this public repo would defeat that by putting it in git history
# instead. content/resume/ is where a future real download PDF gets generated
# from; that PDF is the intended public artifact, not this source.
content/resume/
